<h2>Where should the filter controls go on Account activity?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Wireframes only. Which controls go in the bar is a separate question; these show placement. Click one to select it.</p>

<div class="options">
  <div class="option" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">A</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Filter bar between the intro and the table</h3>
      <p>Labeled controls in one row, wrapping on narrow screens. A result count sits under the bar. Always visible, nothing to open.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;font-size:.85rem">Event type<input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;font-size:.85rem">Date range<input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;font-size:.85rem">Search<input class="mock-input" value="" placeholder="device, location, details" readonly></label>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:.8rem">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">B</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>Quick filters plus the bar</h3>
      <p>Same bar as A, with a "Show" radio group on top: All events / Failed sign-ins / Account changes. The failed sign-ins case that support tickets ask about is one click.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:.5rem;font-size:.85rem">
            <strong>Show</strong>
            <span>(o) All events</span><span>( ) Failed sign-ins</span><span>( ) Account changes</span>
          </div>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;font-size:.85rem">Event type<input class="mock-input" value="All events" readonly></label>
            <label style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.25rem;font-size:.85rem">Date range<input class="mock-input" value="Last 90 days" readonly></label>
          </div>
          <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:.8rem">Showing 48 of 48 events</p>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="option" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="letter">C</div>
    <div class="content">
      <h3>"Filter" button opening a panel</h3>
      <p>A button above the table opens a popover with the controls. Active filters show as removable tags. Takes the least room, but every filter is one extra click.</p>
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">Account activity</div>
        <div class="mockup-body">
          <p style="margin:0 0 .5rem">Every sign-in and account change from the last 90 days, newest first.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <button class="mock-button">Filter</button>
            <span style="font-size:.8rem;border:1px solid currentColor;border-radius:1rem;padding:0 .5rem">Sign-in failed  x</span>
            <span style="font-size:.8rem">Showing 6 of 48 events</span>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder">Table: When | Event | Device | Location | IP | Details</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
